# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Everything here is optional — the site runs
# without any of it, but forms and card payments stay in fallback mode.

# --- Forms -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Formspree form ids (https://formspree.io — free tier is fine to start).
# Create one form for orders and one for general enquiries, then paste the ids.
# Without these, the contact form and checkout fall back to a mailto: draft,
# or to "please call the shop" when no email address is set below.
VITE_FORMSPREE_ORDER_ID=
VITE_FORMSPREE_CONTACT_ID=

# The shop's public email address. The existing site doesn't publish one, so
# this is intentionally blank until Fisher Firearms confirm it.
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# --- Payments ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Stripe publishable key (pk_live_... / pk_test_...).
# While this is empty the checkout runs in clearly-labelled demo mode: no card
# is taken, the order is just sent to the shop.
#
# IMPORTANT: Stripe's prohibited-business rules cover firearms, ammunition and
# certain parts. Only genuinely shippable accessories, optics and gift
# certificates should ever be charged online — the catalogue's `saleType`
# already enforces this, and firearms/ammo are always reserve-only.
VITE_STRIPE_PK=
